# UI status is a first-class implementation concern

(Adrian, 2026-10-16.) Any change to **index / hydrate / boot / catch-up / jobs / health** must ship matching **user-visible status in the same change**. Do not treat status chrome as a follow-up PR.

Ship all of these when the process is user-visible:

- **Status bar**
- **`IndexStatusReporter`** (Settings Index card **and** search-modal footer)
- **Progress with known units** — files `done/total` or `%` — when the process has them

Do **not** leave the user on a static label with no motion (`Starting up`, `Hydrating`, and similar) while work is running. If units exist, show them updating.
